comments:
I can confirm that there is indeed a problem. Here is a much simpler repo:
```c#
var a = new List<object>();
var b = new List<string>();

a.Add("test");
b.Add("test");

Console.WriteLine("a: " + a.AsQueryable().FirstOrDefault(x => false));
Console.WriteLine("b: " + b.AsQueryable().FirstOrDefault(x => false));
```

In both cases we should have the console print `null`, but instead when we're querying against the `object` list, the first item is returned.

It seems `LastOrDefault` ~~doesn't~~ also has this problem.

